  "title": "Bodies and sense-making are irreducibly historical",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "3da9f5e8-3452-4546-b81d-fc8ad217bcb8",
      "text": "Enaction conceives of bodies and sense-making as irreducibly historical, depending on the past and changing the present, and co-constituted by the sociomaterial world in ways that go far beyond the processing of information. This is a reading of the slogan laying down a path in walking.",
